      "conditions": {
        "title": "What does Conditions mean?",
        "content": "Conditions describe rules and thresholds for each column in the table. Each column has a data source (where data comes from), optional formula (how values are calculated), and conditions that control color coding and filtering. Green = good, blue = medium, red = bad."
      },
      "filters": {
        "title": "How filtering works",
        "content": "You can filter in two ways: 1) Column filters – click the filter icon in the column header to filter directly in that column. 2) Advanced filters – open the filter menu to combine multiple conditions. Column filters and advanced filters can be combined."
      },
      "score": {
